// src/v4/lens/complexity.dag
//
// Scope: complexity lens — structural fact carried by data model, not behavioral test.
// Anchor: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computational_complexity_theory + https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_O_notation
// Unifies: (per THESIS:187) coercion cost = complexity. The cost of converting between representations IS a complexity-lens read; no parallel CoercionCost carrier. A worker computing coercion cost reads via this lens.
//
// U2 (operator-ratified 2026-05-15): this lens is the asymptotic
// PROJECTION of `lens/cost.dag`'s SymbolicCost — it CONSUMES that
// carrier and never independently re-derives cost. One mechanism, two
// projections (SymbolicCost = the realization-cost expression;
// ComplexityBound = its asymptotic class). Re-deriving here would create
// a second cost authority — forbidden (the parallel-authority bug U1/U2
// foreclose).
//
// Owns:
//   - Complexity dimension type
//   - lens read: Node -> Witness<ComplexityBound>
//     (the asymptotic projection of cost.dag's SymbolicCost — consumed,
//     not re-derived)
//   - reads program structure; no heuristic, no escape
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag, std/witness.dag, std/diagnostic.dag
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-12


module v4.lens.complexity

